# Model card for reginute1 (medium)

* Language: lt_LT (Lithuanian, Lithuania)
* Speakers: 1
* Quality: medium
* Samplerate: 22,050Hz

## Dataset

* URL: https://huggingface.co/datasets/meldynamics/liepa-tts
* License: CC-BY-4.0

LIEPA corpus, Vilnius University. Speaker Regina Jokubauskaitė (professional
actress), studio recordings, 5 121 utterances, ~3 hours. Stress and pitch
accents in the training transcriptions come from the corpus' own annotation,
sentence by sentence.

## Training

Fine-tuned from the Piper catalogue checkpoint `ru_RU-irina-medium`
(`rhasspy/piper-checkpoints`), which is itself fine-tuned from
`en_US-lessac-medium`. Training data licence is CC-BY-4.0; the lineage above is
stated so that the base-model question (see piper-voices discussion #94) is
visible rather than hidden.

## Phonemization — please read

This voice uses `phoneme_type: text` with a custom `phoneme_id_map`
(IPA + three Lithuanian accent marks `ˈ ˌ ˋ`). It does **not** use espeak-ng at
synthesis time, because espeak-ng misplaces Lithuanian stress in roughly half
of the words against the corpus' gold annotation.

Text must therefore be phonemized by `phonemize_lithuanian.py` (shipped with
the voice; proposed as a `PhonemeType.LITHUANIAN` contribution to piper1-gpl)
together with the stress dictionary `lt_kirciai.tsv`. Plain Piper without the
phonemizer feeds the model raw letters and will not produce Lithuanian.

Recommended: `normalize_audio=False` (the default `True` clips this voice).

